          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em successor
            of something is the thing one step after it.
          %h2#successors_of_natural_numbers Successors of natural numbers
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+number"} natural number
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %strong successor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n^+
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            is simply
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n + 1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers+object"} natural numbers object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
            is equipped with a successor morphism
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}\to\mathbb{N}
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1\to \mathbb{N}
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/recursion"} recursion
          %p
            The formula
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi n
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n^+ \coloneqq n + 1
            may be usefully generalized to other types of numbers; for example, in the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/golden+ratio"} golden ratio
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Φ
                  %mo ≈
                  %mn 0.618
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi \approx 0.618
            is the positive number whose successor equals its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reciprocal"} reciprocal
            (or more commonly, the golden ratio
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo ≈
                  %mn 1.618
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \approx 1.618
            is the common successor and reciprocal of
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Φ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
          %h2#successors_in_wellorderings_and_cardinals Successors in well-orderings and cardinals
          %p
            Generalizing successors in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well-ordered+set"} well-ordered set
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %strong successor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi w
                    %mo +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w^+
            of an element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi w
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w
            is the least element of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            which is (strictly) greater than
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi w
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w
            (if such an element exists). If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            has no
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maximal+element"} maximal element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi w
                  %mo ↦
                  %msup
                    %mi w
                    %mo +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w \mapsto w^+
            is always defined; it is sometimes used to make recursive definitions. We say that an element of a well-ordered set
            %em is a successor
            if it is the successor of something.
          %p
            This notion is sometimes also used for some well-ordered proper classes, for example for the classes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Ord
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Ord}
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinal+number"} ordinal number
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Card
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Card
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cardinal+numbers"} cardinal numbers
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
            %strong successor ordinal
            of an ordinal
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            is the least ordinal greater than
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo ∪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \cup \{\alpha\}
            %strong successor cardinal
            of a cardinal
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi κ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            is the least cardinal greater than
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
          %p
            Note that if we identify a cardinal number with the least ordinal having that cardinality, as is common in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/material+set+theory"} material set theory
            %em successor ordinal
            and the
            %em successor cardinal
            of that cardinal are different. For instance, the successor ordinal of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi ℵ
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega = \aleph_0
            is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega+1
            (which is not a cardinal), whereas its successor cardinal is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℵ
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \aleph_1
            (which is an ordinal but not a successor ordinal).
          %p
            For definitions by
            = succeed "," do
              %span.newWikiWord
                transfinite recursion
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/transfinite+recursion"} ?
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/von+Neumann+hierarchy"} von Neumann hierarchy
            of well-founded
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pure+set"} pure set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            must) also handle all three cases at once, and the successor function is used there as well.
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi α
                    %mo +
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi α
                  %mo ∪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi α
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha^+ \coloneqq \alpha \cup \{\alpha\}
            again, but it's not clear in what sense this is the smallest ordinal strictly greater than
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truth+value"} truth value
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi α
                    %mi P
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi α
                  %mo ∪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi α
                  %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ∣
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha_P \coloneqq \alpha \cup \{\alpha \mid P\}
            satisfies
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo ≤
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mi P
                    %mo ≤
                    %msup
                      %mi α
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \leq \alpha_P \leq \alpha^+
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi α
                    %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha_P
            equals either
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            or
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi α
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha^+
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi α
                    %mi P
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\alpha_P)^+
            is provably strictly greater than
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            in a sense, but we cannot prove that
            = succeed ".)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi α
                      %mo +
                    %mo ≤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mi P
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha^+ \leq (\alpha_P)^+
          %h2#successors_of_material_sets Successors of material sets
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/material+set+theory"} material set theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi α
                    %mo +
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi α
                  %mo ∪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi α
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha^+ \coloneqq \alpha \cup \{\alpha\}
            is generalized from von Neumann ordinals to arbitrary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pure+sets"} pure sets
            (or material sets with
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/urelements"} urelements
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mo +
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi X
                  %mo ∪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^+ \coloneqq X \cup \{X\}
            of a material set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is the smallest material set that contains
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            as both a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
            and a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/member"} member
